# Config and tests

## YAML structure

```yaml
settings:
  dry_run: bool
  duplicate_detection: bool   # default true
  bootstrap_folders: bool     # default true

paths:                        # all keys required
  downloads_dir: ...
  auto_archive_dir: ...
  trash_later_dir: ...
  to_review_dir: ...
  media_incoming_dir: ...
  media_assets_dir: ...
  log_file: ...

bootstrap_dirs:               # optional list of extra folders
  - ~/Projects/Active

rules:
  pdf:
    archive_after_days: 30
    trash_after_days: 90
    delete_after_days: 120
  mp4:
    route: media              # media | media_assets | review | archive

default:
  route: review
  archive_after_days: 14
```

Thresholds must be ascending: archive < trash < delete. Review route requires `archive_after_days`.

## Test patterns

```python
from conftest import make_config, reload_download_manager, set_file_age_days

# Isolated config via env var
dm = reload_download_manager(monkeypatch, config_path)
set_file_age_days(path, 31)  # simulate aged file
dm.main()
```

Use `tmp_path` fixtures — never touch real `~/Downloads` in tests.

## Verification before completion

```bash
.venv/bin/pytest tests/ -v
```
